      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Nagahori Tsurumi-ryokuchi Line became Japan’s first linear‑motor rapid transit system when it opened in 1990.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagahori_Tsurumi-ryokuchi_Line",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Initially called the Tsurumi‑ryokuchi Line, the route ran from Kyōbashi to Tsurumi‑ryokuchi and later adopted the name of the park and Nagahori‑dori avenue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagahori_Tsurumi-ryokuchi_Line",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "From 1972, the low‑lying Tsurumi area served as Osaka’s largest landfill, dumping solid waste and sewage sludge before becoming a park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lawrencetravelstories.com/eng-tsurumi-ku-osaka-navigating-the-strata-from-ancient-wetlands-to-world-expo/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hidden beneath the park, small methane vent pipes quietly release gases produced by the decomposing landfill beneath the ground.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lawrencetravelstories.com/eng-tsurumi-ku-osaka-navigating-the-strata-from-ancient-wetlands-to-world-expo/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Enomoto Shrine stands as the spiritual anchor of Tsurumi’s wetland heritage, tracing back to the region’s ancient marshlands.",
